A||||14||rodmcneill||Heading out to Vegas.||||1||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||09-25-2001||01:49 PM||||Leaving tomorrow for one week for a trade show-vacation. Will be staying at the Stratosphere(tallest building west of the Mississippi) mmmm.... It has a rollercoaster right on top of it and another ride that shoots you straight up. If I can pluck up enough courage I might try it. Looking forward to the vacation, probably check out Hoover Dam, Zion National Park. Besides all the casinos any other recommendations for places to visit? I will be interested to see how many people are flying and what kind of airport security they will have.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Blondie88||09-25-2001||02:00 PM||||Well absolutely! I'm sure you'll have tons of fun in Vegas, I've been there many a times, actually lived there for a year.  The stratosphere ride is really fun, and it doesn't take that much will-power to do it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  You should go on "big shot" it's not the rollercoaster, but the thing that shoots you up, you can see ALL of las vegas, it's the best.  <P>As for other things to do, there are always those touristy things like the pirate show at the Treasure Island and the coreographed fountains at the Bellagio.  If you go to the Aladdin you can even see belly dancers and stuff.  I really recommend though that you take in a show, it's a sin not to see a show in Vegas!  I'd go to the luxor and see the blue man group.  Awesome music, hilarious and just wild and crazy fun!  <P>I saw the vargas fight on HBO the other day and when they spanned Vegas, it was dead!  There was hardly anyone on the streets, it seemed so peculiar.  If you want to see the hoover dam and all that fun stuff, then I would recommend also taking one of those helicopter tours, they look pretty fun, if they're able to fly!  <P>Sorry I ran on for so long, if you have any questions about the sin city, i'm pretty well read up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Have fun!||||reg||1
Z||000002||EdsB52||09-25-2001||02:40 PM||||I go there several times a year, including the weekend before last. I would suggest the coaster at the Nascar Cafe. It's at the Sahara Hotel. They claim 0-70 in 3 seconds, and I believe it. It leaves the building, goes out to the strip and turns parallel to it, shoots down through the sidewalk, comes out and does a loop, goes through the Sahara sign, and turns off the strip and goes vertical like the Superman ride. Then of course it does the whole thing backwards again. Buy a day pass for 13 bucks, you'll want to go again and ride in the front at least once.<P>Go out of town and check out the Mustang Ranch! I've never been there. New York New York is cool. Check out the inside of it. It's by far the most ornate casino in Vegas. As far as the flight; be ready for a cavity search. Not exactly, but just about.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Blondie88||09-25-2001||04:21 PM||||haha mustang ranch...good choice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  That's famous for the best prostitutes around, besides the pussycat saloon in Northern Nevada.  Of course, there are a couple different mustang ranches, and if that's not the one your thinking then....prostitues? What are prostitutes? ||||reg||4
Z||000004||JSocha||09-25-2001||05:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Blondie88:<BR><B>haha mustang ranch...good choice   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  That's famous for the best prostitutes around, besides the pussycat saloon in Northern Nevada.  Of course, there are a couple different mustang ranches, and if that's not the one your thinking then....prostitues? What are prostitutes? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was going to share a "really, really, really" bad joke about these ranches.  I think though I will hold off because as I said, it is "really, really, really" that bad.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||IwannaIRM||09-25-2001||06:56 PM||||A little FYI.  The Mustang Ranch isn't located near Las Vegas.  The real Mustang ranch was East of Reno.  It would be a long drive from LV to just go and see the Mustang Ranch.<P>Actually all that is really there is a bunch of mobile homes out back of a bar.  Even then most of them should be gone since the Mustang Ranch was shut down by the Feds 2 years ago.<P>How many here knew that the Mustang Ranch actually had a listing on the NYSE?  They went public so to speak!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Blondie88||09-25-2001||07:03 PM||||Good show, that's the one I was thinking about.  I read in the newspaper that one of the prostitutes was leaking information to spies or something hahaha everyone says i'm full of it, but I really read it in the Reno Gazette!  If it really isn't true...it's still kinda interesting to think about. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rick 88||09-25-2001||07:41 PM||||If you haven't gotten enough cars, check out the Imperial Palace Auto Museum on the Strip.<BR>Also Carrol Shelby's factory is there and a neat place to see. Your week will be up before you know it! No time for  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"><P>Rick 88||||reg||3
Z||000008||Jimmy||09-25-2001||10:21 PM||||Go to, Voodoo Cafe its on the top of the RIO.  Also check out the cocktail lounge outside at Harrahs, the bartenders are awesome(flip all the bottles around and stuff) plus on fridays/saturdays Cokkie Jarr is performing(Best free lounge act in town).  Have fun<P>Jim(goes to vegas twice a year)||||reg||1
Z||000009||EdsB52||09-26-2001||03:34 AM||||Check out Race Rock (I think). It's located downtown at the East end of the covered street. They have monster trucks, road race bikes, drag cars, and even a BD-5 hanging up in there. It's very cool and they have good food. I haven't been there for a while, but I believe it's still there.||||reg||1
Z||000010||firstfiero||09-26-2001||10:01 AM||||     I love vegas!!! I got married their and went again 6 months ago to the domino's convention. New york new york roller coaster kicks ass. Theirs so much to do beside gambling that you will have a to do list a mile long! Both times I wanted to see a show and just didn't get to it. Hopefully my franchisee will spring for my wife and I to go to the convention again. Nothing like a free to vegas. We stayed at excalibur this last time. It was  nice but not as nice as the golden nugget. It's the only hotel thats still first class on fairmont street.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Doni Hagan||09-26-2001||10:35 AM||||Hey, Rod...<P>Drop by the studio when you get back. Have a safe trip and bring me back a souvenier (preferably a few rolls of silver dollars!)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||EdsB52||09-26-2001||11:30 AM||||I heard Jay Leno was going to be performing there this weekend. The show is free if you have a room key and an out of state drivers license (why I don't know). I don't know which venue he'll be at, but ask arond.||||reg||1
Z||000013||starfighter007@msn.com||09-26-2001||12:46 PM||||I just got back from there on monday my wife and I drove up saturday afternoon from phx.Still very scared to get on a plane. I did notice that there were a lot of people there but I understand that most of those people are locals.I noticed that maybe 75% of the resturants were empty.We ate at the Rio buffet saturday night there was a 30 minute wait to get in.And I highly recommend that you go there at least once.hope you have a nice trip <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||Rick 88||09-26-2001||01:08 PM||||Leno's going to be at the MGM Grand. Better get there way early!<P>Rick 88||||reg||4
